text:
Noah: heads up 5min ago I noticed the primary CTA on the new dashboard uses a fade for the pressed state. on emulated 3G it feels like the button lags and users can trigger the action twice by double-tapping. screenshot + recording in thread.

Rina: can reproduce. the UI currently toggles a `.pressed` class after the opacity transition finishes which explains the delay. also no client-side debounce.

Theo: suggestion: switch to an immediate transform scale for press-down (instant), then animate release with easing. that keeps tactile feel without blocking events.

Jules: agree. plus add a 200-300ms debounce on actionable buttons client-side. small enough to not disrupt power users, long enough to prevent accidental duplicates. I'll prototype CSS and a tiny JS helper: ```js
function withDebounce(el, fn, wait=250){
  let locked = false;
  el.addEventListener('click', e=>{
    if(locked) return;
    locked = true;
    fn(e);
    setTimeout(()=> locked = false, wait);
  });
}
```

Noah: also seeing duplicate toasts when network is flaky. propose we coalesce identical toasts for a short window (800-1000ms) to reduce noise.

Rina: accessibility checklist: toasts should live in a region with `role=status` and `aria-live=polite`; ensure we set `aria-atomic=true` and avoid moving focus. for buttons the pressed look is purely presentational unless toggle behavior exists 5 don't set `aria-pressed` unless it's a toggle.

Theo: good call. copy-wise, let's standardize short affirmative toasts: single-word verbs like `Saved`, `Sent`, `Deleted`. longer copy reserved for error details or info banners.

Jules: implementation plan: 1) swap CSS to instant press + release animation (design + frontend) 2) add debounce helper and apply to primary CTAs 3) client toast coalescing library 4) telemetry events `ux.button.down`, `ux.button.action_emitted`, `ux.toast.coalesced` 5) small canary rollout to 10% traffic. estimate 2 dev days + 1 design day.

Noah: priority high for dashboard since it impacts first-time impressions. Rina can you own the CSS animation? Jules please do debounce + toast work. Theo please update copy tokens in the design system docs.

Rina: taking CSS. will mock motion in Figma and add token recommendations (press-duration: 0ms, release-ease: 120ms cubic-bezier).

Jules: opening WIP PR, adding unit tests for debounce and toast coalescing. also will add a flag `feature.ui.coalesce_toasts` so we can flip during rollout.

aria-bot: created issue #4399: button-press-lag-and-toast-duplicates, assigned to @rina and @jules.

Theo: one tiny note: backend should still be idempotent for important actions. debounce is UX guard only. add a line to API design checklist.

Noah: perfect. after landing let's run a short experiment measuring duplicate action rate and toast counts per session. thanks all.
